.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt NOVI-HOTPLUG 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm novi-hotplug
.Nd handle a kernel uevent
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the handler busybox
.Nm uevent
runs for each event on the kernel's netlink stream.
It applies the same modalias-to-
modprobe(8)
rule
.Xr novi-hwdetect 8
applies to a directory walk, initialises a sound card that has just
appeared, and calls
.Xr novi-mount 8
for a block device.
.Pp
It reads the environment the kernel supplies
.Pf ( Ev ACTION ,
.Ev SUBSYSTEM ,
.Ev DEVPATH ,
.Ev MODALIAS )
and is not run by hand.
.Ss Nothing in the handler may block
The listener runs the handler with
.Fn spawn_and_wait ,
so a slow handler stalls the queue but loses nothing \(em which is
the right trade, and the reason the listener forces a 128 MB netlink
receive buffer: events queue in the kernel during a burst rather
than being dropped.
But a handler that
.Em blocks
stops the queue indefinitely, which is why the
.Xr alsactl 1
call and the mount are backgrounded.
.Ss What it does not do
.Nm
does not touch networking.
An interface that appears after boot gets a driver and no lease,
because the network service picks one interface at start.
Per-interface DHCP is the network service's problem; reaching into it
from a uevent handler is split-brain.
.Pp
.Nm mdev
is deliberately unused.
devtmpfs creates the device nodes in the kernel before any of this
runs, and mdev would be a second creator with its own rule file to
keep in sync.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
Set by the kernel:
.Ev ACTION ,
.Ev SUBSYSTEM ,
.Ev DEVPATH ,
.Ev DEVNAME ,
.Ev MODALIAS .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr novi-hwdetect 8 ,
.Xr novi-mount 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 0012.
.Sh CAVEATS
.Nm alsactl init
exits
.Sy 99
on success.
.Dq Hardware is initialized using a generic method
plus exit 99 is the documented path for a card no ruleset matches,
and it did initialise.
Do not
.Dq fix
the 99.
.Pp
It also knows only standard mixer control names, so a card that
invents its own \(em QEMU's emulated USB audio does \(em stays muted.
That is why the handler
.Em logs
that it called alsactl: whether it ran and whether it worked are
separate questions.
